   "surprises": [
    {
     "claim": "The average new car weighs a bit over 4,000 pounds, about 4,300 or more by recent EPA data (4,354 lb per the EPA's 2025 Automotive Trends Report).",
     "role": "stakes",
     "search": "average new car weight pounds EPA trends report"
    },
    {
     "claim": "Bags usually top out around 100 psi, and the tank is typically filled to about 150-200 psi.",
     "role": "fix2",
     "search": "air suspension tank pressure 150 200 psi bags 100 psi"
    },
    {
     "claim": "A bag with an effective diameter of about six inches, at 100 psi, supports roughly 2,800 pounds. Real bags give a bit less, depending on their shape and height.",
     "role": "fact",
     "search": "air bag 6 inch diameter 100 psi load capacity pounds"
    }
   ]
  },
  "sentences": [
   {
    "role": "hook",
    "text": "If you swap a car's steel springs for rubber bags of air, you have air suspension."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem",
    "text": "But a bag leaks and goes flat, and the car sags down onto its tires."
   },
   {
    "role": "stakes",
    "text": "Now over 4,000 pounds of car press down on a flat bag that cannot hold it."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix1",
    "text": "So you add a compressor that pumps air down a hose into the bag, and the car lifts."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem2",
    "text": "But the little pump is slow, so after every bump the car sinks and stays low."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix2",
    "text": "So you add a tank filled to about 150 to 200 pounds per square inch, and the bag refills in seconds."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem3",
    "text": "But now the tank's air rushes in, the bag swells, and the car shoots up too high."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix3",
    "text": "So you add a valve that lets air in or out, and the car settles at the right height."
   },
   {
    "role": "name",
    "text": "This bag is called an air spring."
   },
   {
    "role": "name2",
    "text": "And the bag, pump, tank and valve together are called air suspension."
   },
   {
    "role": "how",
    "text": "The compressor fills the tank, the valve opens, and air lifts the car."
   },
   {
    "role": "fact",
    "text": "At 100 pounds per square inch, a bag about six inches across holds roughly 2,800 pounds."
   },
   {
    "role": "finish",
    "text": "Add a remote with a height button and a pressure light."
   },
   {
    "role": "congrats",
    "text": "Congratulations, you have built a bagged car."
   }
  ],
